{"entries":[{"title":"Untitled","url":"/configuration/index.html","content":"Skip to main content Skip to content FeaturesPostsExplore by tagContact Us 🇬🇧 English 🇫🇷 Français 🇸🇦 العربية 🇧🇩 বাংলা 🇨🇿 Čeština 🇩🇪 Deutsch 🇪🇸 Español 🇳🇬 Hausa 🇮🇱 עברית 🇮🇳 हिन्दी 🇮🇩 Indonesia 🇮🇹 Italiano 🇯🇵 日本語 🇰🇷 한국어 🇳🇱 Nederlands 🇵🇱 Polski 🇵🇹 Português 🇷🇴 Română 🇷🇺 Русский 🇸🇪 Svenska 🇹🇭 ไทย 🇵🇭 Filipino 🇹🇷 Türkçe 🇺🇦 Українська 🇻🇳 Tiếng Việt 🇳🇬 Yorùbá 🇨🇳 简体中文 🇹🇼 繁體中文 Home>Configuration Reference Configuration Reference Configuration file Polaris reads ~/.config/polaris/config.toml on start. CLI flags override file values. Env vars override both. [auth] method = \"oauth\" # \"oauth\" | \"token\" | \"iam\" cache_credentials = true [server] endpoint = \"https://api.polaris.example.com\" timeout_seconds = 30 [output] format = \"table\" # \"table\" | \"json\" | \"csv\" colour = \"auto\" # \"auto\" | \"always\" | \"never\" Environment variables Variable Default Purpose POLARIS_TOKEN — Override the cached OAuth token POLARIS_ENDPOINT https://api.polaris.example.com Override the API endpoint POLARIS_TIMEOUT 30 Per-request timeout in seconds POLARIS_FORMAT table Default output format POLARIS_NO_COLOUR unset Disable ANSI colour in output CLI flags Flags accepted by every command: --endpoint <URL> — override the configured endpoint --format <table|json|csv> — override the output format --quiet — suppress informational logging --verbose — include debug logging on stderr","headings":["Configuration Reference","Configuration file","Environment variables","CLI flags"]},{"title":"Untitled","url":"/contact/index.html","content":"Skip to main content Skip to content FeaturesPostsExplore by tagContact Us 🇬🇧 English 🇫🇷 Français 🇸🇦 العربية 🇧🇩 বাংলা 🇨🇿 Čeština 🇩🇪 Deutsch 🇪🇸 Español 🇳🇬 Hausa 🇮🇱 עברית 🇮🇳 हिन्दी 🇮🇩 Indonesia 🇮🇹 Italiano 🇯🇵 日本語 🇰🇷 한국어 🇳🇱 Nederlands 🇵🇱 Polski 🇵🇹 Português 🇷🇴 Română 🇷🇺 Русский 🇸🇪 Svenska 🇹🇭 ไทย 🇵🇭 Filipino 🇹🇷 Türkçe 🇺🇦 Українська 🇻🇳 Tiếng Việt 🇳🇬 Yorùbá 🇨🇳 简体中文 🇹🇼 繁體中文 Home>Support Support Get help General support: support@polaris.example.com Security disclosures: security@polaris.example.com (PGP key: download) Partnerships: partners@polaris.example.com Response times Channel First response Resolution target Free tier 3 business days best effort Pro tier 1 business day 5 business days Enterprise 4 hours per contract Status page Live operational status: https://status.polaris.example.com","headings":["Support","Get help","Response times","Status page"]},{"title":"Untitled","url":"/getting-started/index.html","content":"Skip to main content Skip to content FeaturesPostsExplore by tagContact Us 🇬🇧 English 🇫🇷 Français 🇸🇦 العربية 🇧🇩 বাংলা 🇨🇿 Čeština 🇩🇪 Deutsch 🇪🇸 Español 🇳🇬 Hausa 🇮🇱 עברית 🇮🇳 हिन्दी 🇮🇩 Indonesia 🇮🇹 Italiano 🇯🇵 日本語 🇰🇷 한국어 🇳🇱 Nederlands 🇵🇱 Polski 🇵🇹 Português 🇷🇴 Română 🇷🇺 Русский 🇸🇪 Svenska 🇹🇭 ไทย 🇵🇭 Filipino 🇹🇷 Türkçe 🇺🇦 Українська 🇻🇳 Tiếng Việt 🇳🇬 Yorùbá 🇨🇳 简体中文 🇹🇼 繁體中文 Home>Getting Started Getting Started Install Polaris ships as a single binary. Install with your platform's package manager: # macOS brew install polaris # Linux (Debian/Ubuntu) apt install polaris # Windows winget install Polaris.CLI Authenticate polaris auth login This opens a browser window to your account; the resulting token is stored in ~/.config/polaris/credentials.toml. Make your first request polaris query \"select count(*) from events\" If the command returns a number, you're set. If it errors, jump to the Configuration reference for connection settings, or contact support if the error is unfamiliar.","headings":["Getting Started","Install","Authenticate","Make your first request"]},{"title":"Untitled","url":"/index.html","content":"Skip to main content Skip to content FeaturesPostsExplore by tagContact Us🇬🇧 English 🇫🇷 Français 🇸🇦 العربية 🇧🇩 বাংলা 🇨🇿 Čeština 🇩🇪 Deutsch 🇪🇸 Español 🇳🇬 Hausa 🇮🇱 עברית 🇮🇳 हिन्दी 🇮🇩 Indonesia 🇮🇹 Italiano 🇯🇵 日本語 🇰🇷 한국어 🇳🇱 Nederlands 🇵🇱 Polski 🇵🇹 Português 🇷🇴 Română 🇷🇺 Русский 🇸🇪 Svenska 🇹🇭 ไทย 🇵🇭 Filipino 🇹🇷 Türkçe 🇺🇦 Українська 🇻🇳 Tiếng Việt 🇳🇬 Yorùbá 🇨🇳 简体中文 🇹🇼 繁體中文PolarisPolaris — a documentation template you can adapt.Get Started Learn MoreWelcomePolaris is a documentation template you can clone, edit, and ship as the docs site for any developer tool, library, or API. The structure is opinionated; the content is yours to replace.What's in this templateGetting started — install + first run, in under a pageConfiguration reference — every option, in a single scannable tableAPI reference — endpoint + method tables with examplesRelease notes — chronological changelog, surfaced via the Posts pageBrowse by topic — automatic tag aggregation across every pageContact — support routing for users who can't find an answerHow to use itClone this directoryReplace every page in content/ with your own copyUpdate brand colour, logo URL, and footer copyright in the frontmatterBuild with cargo run --example docsDeploy the contents of examples/docs/public/ to any static hostThat's it. The plugins, sitemap, search index, and accessibility report all work without further configuration.","headings":["Polaris","Welcome","What's in this template","How to use it"]},{"title":"Untitled","url":"/plugin-api/index.html","content":"Skip to main content Skip to content FeaturesPostsExplore by tagContact Us 🇬🇧 English 🇫🇷 Français 🇸🇦 العربية 🇧🇩 বাংলা 🇨🇿 Čeština 🇩🇪 Deutsch 🇪🇸 Español 🇳🇬 Hausa 🇮🇱 עברית 🇮🇳 हिन्दी 🇮🇩 Indonesia 🇮🇹 Italiano 🇯🇵 日本語 🇰🇷 한국어 🇳🇱 Nederlands 🇵🇱 Polski 🇵🇹 Português 🇷🇴 Română 🇷🇺 Русский 🇸🇪 Svenska 🇹🇭 ไทย 🇵🇭 Filipino 🇹🇷 Türkçe 🇺🇦 Українська 🇻🇳 Tiếng Việt 🇳🇬 Yorùbá 🇨🇳 简体中文 🇹🇼 繁體中文 Home>API Reference API Reference Base URL https://api.polaris.example.com/v1 All routes use JSON. Pass a bearer token to log in. Endpoints Method Path Purpose GET /datasets List datasets you can read GET /datasets/{id} Get one dataset's metadata POST /datasets/{id}/queries Run a query on a dataset GET /queries/{id} Poll a query for results DELETE /queries/{id} Cancel a running query Example: submit a query curl -X POST \\ -H \"Authorization: Bearer $POLARIS_TOKEN\" \\ -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\ -d '{\"sql\": \"select count(*) from events\"}' \\ https://api.polaris.example.com/v1/datasets/my-dataset/queries Response: { \"query_id\": \"q_01HZ2K9X8R7Y6V5T4S3R2Q1P0\", \"status\": \"running\", \"submitted_at\": \"<DATE>\" } Error codes Code Meaning 400 Bad JSON, bad SQL, or missing field 401 Missing or expired token 403 Token valid but no access to this dataset 404 Dataset or query ID not found 429 Rate limit hit — see Retry-After header 500 Server error — please report it","headings":["API Reference","Base URL","Endpoints","Example: submit a query","Error codes"]},{"title":"Untitled","url":"/posts/index.html","content":"Skip to main content Skip to content FeaturesPostsExplore by tagContact Us 🇬🇧 English 🇫🇷 Français 🇸🇦 العربية 🇧🇩 বাংলা 🇨🇿 Čeština 🇩🇪 Deutsch 🇪🇸 Español 🇳🇬 Hausa 🇮🇱 עברית 🇮🇳 हिन्दी 🇮🇩 Indonesia 🇮🇹 Italiano 🇯🇵 日本語 🇰🇷 한국어 🇳🇱 Nederlands 🇵🇱 Polski 🇵🇹 Português 🇷🇴 Română 🇷🇺 Русский 🇸🇪 Svenska 🇹🇭 ไทย 🇵🇭 Filipino 🇹🇷 Türkçe 🇺🇦 Українська 🇻🇳 Tiếng Việt 🇳🇬 Yorùbá 🇨🇳 简体中文 🇹🇼 繁體中文 Home>Release Notes Release Notes Release notes Polaris ships every two weeks. Subscribe to the RSS feed or Atom feed for release announcements. v2.4.0 — 16 April 2026 Added support for streaming query results via Server-Sent Events Changed default output format from json to table for query command Fixed OAuth token refresh failing on tokens issued before v2.0 v2.3.0 — 2 April 2026 Added --format=csv output mode Added polaris datasets describe <id> command Deprecated polaris list (use polaris datasets instead; will be removed in v3.0) v2.2.1 — 19 March 2026 Fixed rate-limit handling: client now respects Retry-After headers Fixed crash on Windows when terminal didn't support ANSI colour","headings":["Release Notes","Release notes","v2.4.0 — 16 April 2026","v2.3.0 — 2 April 2026","v2.2.1 — 19 March 2026"]},{"title":"Untitled","url":"/privacy/index.html","content":"Skip to main content Skip to content FeaturesPostsExplore by tagContact Us 🇬🇧 English 🇫🇷 Français 🇸🇦 العربية 🇧🇩 বাংলা 🇨🇿 Čeština 🇩🇪 Deutsch 🇪🇸 Español 🇳🇬 Hausa 🇮🇱 עברית 🇮🇳 हिन्दी 🇮🇩 Indonesia 🇮🇹 Italiano 🇯🇵 日本語 🇰🇷 한국어 🇳🇱 Nederlands 🇵🇱 Polski 🇵🇹 Português 🇷🇴 Română 🇷🇺 Русский 🇸🇪 Svenska 🇹🇭 ไทย 🇵🇭 Filipino 🇹🇷 Türkçe 🇺🇦 Українська 🇻🇳 Tiếng Việt 🇳🇬 Yorùbá 🇨🇳 简体中文 🇹🇼 繁體中文 Home>Privacy Privacy What this site collects This documentation site does not set cookies, run analytics, or include any third-party scripts. Server logs retain IP addresses for 14 days for abuse prevention; nothing else is stored. What the Polaris service collects See the main product privacy notice at https://polaris.example.com/privacy. Deletion To request deletion of your account and all associated data, email privacy@polaris.example.com from the address on file. Deletion is processed within 30 days.","headings":["Privacy","What this site collects","What the Polaris service collects","Deletion"]},{"title":"Untitled","url":"/tags/index.html","content":"Skip to main content Skip to content FeaturesPostsExplore by tagContact Us 🇬🇧 English 🇫🇷 Français 🇸🇦 العربية 🇧🇩 বাংলা 🇨🇿 Čeština 🇩🇪 Deutsch 🇪🇸 Español 🇳🇬 Hausa 🇮🇱 עברית 🇮🇳 हिन्दी 🇮🇩 Indonesia 🇮🇹 Italiano 🇯🇵 日本語 🇰🇷 한국어 🇳🇱 Nederlands 🇵🇱 Polski 🇵🇹 Português 🇷🇴 Română 🇷🇺 Русский 🇸🇪 Svenska 🇹🇭 ไทย 🇵🇭 Filipino 🇹🇷 Türkçe 🇺🇦 Українська 🇻🇳 Tiếng Việt 🇳🇬 Yorùbá 🇨🇳 简体中文 🇹🇼 繁體中文 Home>Browse by Topic Browse by Topic Browse by topic Pick a tag to find related pages. Featured Tags (30) Docs (10 Posts) April 16, 2026: Page Not Found - The page you were looking for doesn't exist. April 16, 2026: Configuration Reference - Configuration reference for Polaris. April 16, 2026: Support - Contact the Polaris team for support, security reports, and partnerships. April 16, 2026: Getting Started - Install Polaris and make your first authenticated request. April 16, 2026: Polaris Documentation - Documentation template for any developer tool, library, or API. Replace the content, keep the structure. April 16, 2026: Offli